{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and motion as separate plants, then use compact specifications to bind each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. The policy strongly favors forward progress in clear space, allows brief random-walk perturbations only after successful forward motion, uses directed one-shot turns for side obstacles, uses a rare one-shot backward escape only for front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front-blocked outcomes.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use decision/action specifications with total uncontrollable transitions and one-shot commit states",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward repeated move_forward, with occasional random_walk only after forward progress",
    "Use conservative obstacle recovery: front -> brief backward escape then directed turn; left -> clockwise turn; right -> counterclockwise turn",
    "Return to forward exploration immediately on path_clear from recovery states",
    "Reserve full_rotate for a dedicated stuck/last_resort path only after repeated front blockage"
  ],
